From 30bbb55fe642fcffce1859bb4b91784c958f6ef3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Berliner <32103696+Styx85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:02:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rocblas: tune the gfx90c HHS_BH TN selection table on gfx90c

Same procedure as for the HB table: re-measure every solution of
Cijk_Alik_Bljk_HHS_BH (FP16 in/out, FP32 accumulation; used e.g. by
PyTorch nn.Linear in half precision) on gfx90c for 1077 of the 1481
vega10 sizes (<= 20 GFLOP, <= 600 MB, >= 2 MFLOP) and a grid of
M, K in {384 ... 8192} x N in {16 ... 2048} (677 new points).

Selected solution vs. old default over 1927 sizes: median 1.66x,
mean 2.1x, >10% faster on 1758 sizes. PyTorch Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B
fp16, 512 sentences: 15.6 s -> 12.6 s, embeddings unchanged
(cosine >= 0.99975 against the CPU reference).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
